UGI study is performed smoothly under fluoroscopy and shows:
> Smooth passage of barium through the esophagus with normal peristalsis, mucosal pattern and profile.
> Visible EG junction in normal position without definite focal lesion. No GE reflux.
> Normal gastric contour and mucosal pattern. No widening and rigidity of the gastric angularis.
> The barium runs fluently through the pyloric canal with good expansion.
> Well-distended duodenal bulb. No definite mucosal thickening detected. 
> The normal C-loop of the duodenum and normal position of the duodenojejunal junction are demonstrated.
)

