::ugism::
(
Barium meal follow-through study is performed smoothly under fluoroscopy and shows:
> Smooth passage of barium through the esophagus with normal peristalsis, mucosal pattern and profile.
> Visible EG junction in normal position without definite focal lesion. No GE reflux.
> Normal gastric contour and mucosal pattern. 
> The barium runs fluently through the pyloric canal with good expansion. Well-distended duodenal bulb.
> The normal C-loop of the duodenum and normal position of the duodenojejunal junction are demonstrated.
> Normal contour of jejunum and ileum without definite focal lesion. 
> The ascending colon is opacified and the ileocecal junction is shown. The appendix is not demonstrated. 
> Total transit time: 90min
)

